WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.250
One short chapter of
the Qur'an, Surah 112.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.830
A hadith says it equals a
third of the whole book.

3
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.570
It ends: And there is none like unto Him.

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.560
Yet Muslims call on God by
many names: the Most Gracious,

5
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.760
the Loving, the Mighty.

6
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.040
Tradition counts ninety-nine.

7
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.620
So if none is like Him, how
can God have so many names?

8
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.350
In this mission, you'll
read the Throne verse,

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.290
recited by many Muslims after
prayer and before sleep.

10
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.960
Then you'll find out which sin Muslims
believe is not forgiven if a person dies

11
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.590
without repenting.

12
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.990
Your mission: find out how one
God, beyond every likeness,

13
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.280
can still be known by many names.
